SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE

The MIT license above covers ONLY the original source code of this repository: the
TypeScript/JavaScript, CSS and configuration files under scripts/, eval/, prototypes/,
design/ and the repository root.

It does NOT cover any file that contains the text of "L'Avenir en commun, édition 2025",
wherever that file lives. Those files are derivative works of a text licensed under
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and are distributed under that same license, with the attribution
"La France insoumise – L'Avenir en commun" (see data/LICENSE). This includes, and is not
limited to:

  data/*.json                       corpus, hashes, stat cards, terms, tags, glossary,
                                    FAQ, riposte, 2022 side corpora
  eval/passages/*.json              extracted passages per glossary term
  eval/questions.json               evaluation set quoting measure ids and texts
  scripts/fixtures/*.html           raw pages saved from melenchon2027.fr
  prototypes/**/data/*.json         runtime projections of the corpus shipped to prototypes
  design/*.md, design/*.json        wherever they quote a measure verbatim
  docs/**                           wherever it quotes a measure verbatim

Because CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 forbids commercial use and requires ShareAlike, those files may not
be relicensed under MIT. A reuser must therefore treat the two sets separately.

THE 2026 EDITION IS NOT LICENSED HERE, AND IS NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY

Since 5 November 2026 the programme is published in a new edition, "L'Avenir en commun — Le
programme de la Nouvelle France". Its publisher's legal notice states that it is NOT under a
Creative Commons licence: it is "© La France insoumise, tous droits réservés". This repository
does not contain its text. Neither the MIT license above nor data/LICENSE grants any right over
it. What the repository does publish about that edition — structure, titles, anchors and
SHA-256 fingerprints — is there so that a quotation can be checked without being republished.

Fonts under design/fonts/ are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (design/fonts/OFL-*.txt).
The logos, posters and illustrations of La France insoumise and of the campaign are NOT
included in this repository and are not licensed here.
